{"id": "fda630c7-e6dd-41a4-b901-0eab8161dcb7", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check this account's Bedrock activity in us-east-1 for the last 14 days. I'm looking for invocations that use a bare foundation-model ID where an inference profile should be used. I'll report back here when I have the results.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_SrTUIZvgrzP3vlQMpQ4eie", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-model-id-audit", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes", "searching-logs", "exploring-metrics", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine whether any Amazon Bedrock model invocations in us-east-1 during the last 14 days used a bare foundation-model ID (e.g. anthropic.claude-...) where an inference profile (system-defined like us.anthropic.claude-... / global.*, or application inference profile ARN) should be used instead. Report which callers (IAM principal/role, source IP/user agent, application) and which model IDs are involved, with call counts and first/last seen times.",
  "context": "User wants a chat answer on whether bare model IDs are used where inference profiles are required or recommended. Note: some newer models can ONLY be invoked via an inference profile in on-demand mode (a bare ID call fails with ValidationException 'on-demand throughput isn't supported'), and others work with bare IDs but cross-region inference profiles are recommended for throughput. Distinguish between (a) calls that FAILED because a bare ID was used where a profile is required, and (b) calls that succeeded with a bare ID where a profile is optional/recommended. Use verify_aws_claim to confirm which models require inference profiles if needed. Bedrock InvokeModel/Converse are generally CloudTrail DATA events (not management events), so check whether data event logging exists (describe trails / event selectors), and also check whether Bedrock model invocation logging is enabled (get_model_invocation_logging_configuration) to CloudWatch Logs or S3 and query it for modelId values. Also check CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics (ModelId dimension) for invocation volume per model ID, which shows whether the dimension is a bare ID or profile ID. Also check Bedrock list_inference_profiles to see which profiles exist. Be explicit about any data-source gaps (e.g. no data event logging or invocation logging means call-level evidence is unavailable) and do not guess.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1", "region us-east-1", "Bedrock InvokeModel, InvokeModelWithResponseStream, Converse, ConverseStream"],
  "timeframe": "Last 14 days ending 2026-11-24T18:55:58Z (start 2026-11-10T18:55:58Z)",
  "criteria": "List every bare model ID observed being invoked, whether each call succeeded or failed, who made it, and whether an inference profile is required or merely recommended for that model. Read-only operations only."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Audit Bedrock model ID usage in us-east-1 over 14 days"}], "created_at": null}

